#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:36
#, xml-text
msgid "&glibc-fin-sbu;"
msgstr "&glibc-fin-sbu;"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><segmentedlist><seglistitem><seg>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:37
#, xml-text
msgid "&glibc-fin-du;"
msgstr "&glibc-fin-du;"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:44
#, xml-text
msgid "Installation of Glibc"
msgstr "Instalação da Glibc"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:50
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Some of the Glibc programs use the non-FHS compliant <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/var/db</filename> directory to store their runtime "
"data. Apply the following patch to make such programs store their runtime "
"data in the FHS-compliant locations:"
msgstr ""
"Alguns dos aplicativos Glibc usam o diretório não conforme com o FHS "
"<filename class=\"directory\">/var/db</filename> para armazenar os dados em "
"tempo de execução deles. Aplique o seguinte remendo para fazer com que tais "
"aplicativos armazenem os dados em tempo de execução deles nos locais "
"conformes com o FHS:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:55
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput remap=\"pre\">patch -Np1 -i ../&glibc-fhs-patch;</userinput>"
msgstr "<userinput remap=\"pre\">patch -Np1 -i ../&glibc-fhs-patch;</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:65
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"The Glibc documentation recommends building Glibc in a dedicated build "
"directory:"
msgstr ""
"A documentação da Glibc recomenda construir a Glibc em um diretório dedicado"
" à construção:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:68
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput remap=\"pre\">mkdir -v build\n"
"cd       build</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput remap=\"pre\">mkdir -v build\n"
"cd      build</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:71
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Ensure that the <command>ldconfig</command> and <command>sln</command> "
"utilities will be installed into <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/usr/sbin</filename>:"
msgstr ""
"Garanta que os utilitários <command>ldconfig</command> e "
"<command>sln</command> serão instalados no <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/usr/sbin</filename>:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:75
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput remap=\"pre\">echo \"rootsbindir=/usr/sbin\" &gt; "
"configparms</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput remap=\"pre\">echo \"rootsbindir=/usr/sbin\" &gt; "
"configparms</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:77
#, xml-text
msgid "Prepare Glibc for compilation:"
msgstr "Prepare a Glibc para compilação:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:79
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput remap=\"configure\">../configure --prefix=/usr                   \\\n"
"             --disable-werror                \\\n"
"             --disable-nscd                  \\\n"
"             libc_cv_slibdir=/usr/lib        \\\n"
"             --enable-stack-protector=strong \\\n"
"             --enable-kernel=&min-kernel;</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput remap=\"configure\">../configure --prefix=/usr                   \\\n"
"             --disable-werror                \\\n"
"             --disable-nscd                  \\\n"
"             libc_cv_slibdir=/usr/lib        \\\n"
"             --enable-stack-protector=strong \\\n"
"             --enable-kernel=&min-kernel;</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><variablelist><title>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:87
#, xml-text
msgid "The meaning of the configure options:"
msgstr "O significado das opções do configure:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:90
#, xml-text
msgid "<parameter>--disable-werror</parameter>"
msgstr "<parameter>--disable-werror</parameter>"

#. type: Content of:
#. <sect1><sect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:92
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"This option disables the -Werror option passed to GCC.  This is necessary "
"for running the test suite."
msgstr ""
"Essa opção desabilita a opção -Werror passada para o GCC. Isso é necessário "
"para executar a suíte de teste."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:98
#, xml-text
msgid "<parameter>--enable-kernel=&min-kernel;</parameter>"
msgstr "<parameter>--enable-kernel=&min-kernel;</parameter>"

#. type: Content of:
#. <sect1><sect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:100
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"This option tells the build system that this Glibc may be used with kernels "
"as old as &min-kernel;. This means generating workarounds in case a system "
"call introduced in a later version cannot be used."
msgstr ""
"Essa opção diz ao sistema de construção que esta Glibc possivelmente seja "
"usada com núcleos tão antigos quanto &min-kernel;. Isso significa que a "
"geração de contornos, no caso de uma chamada de sistema introduzida em uma "
"versão posterior, não pode ser usada."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:108
#, xml-text
msgid "<parameter>--enable-stack-protector=strong</parameter>"
msgstr "<parameter>--enable-stack-protector=strong</parameter>"

#. type: Content of:
#. <sect1><sect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:110
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"This option increases system security by adding extra code to check for "
"buffer overflows, such as stack smashing attacks.  Note that Glibc always "
"explicitly overrides the default of GCC, so this option is still needed even"
" though we've already specified <option>--enable-default-ssp</option> for "
"GCC."
msgstr ""
"Essa opção aumenta a segurança do sistema adicionando código extra para "
"verificar estouros de buffer, como ataques de esmagamento de pilha. Observe "
"que a Glibc sempre substitui explicitamente o padrão do GCC, de forma que "
"essa opção ainda é necessária mesmo que já tenhamos especificado "
"<option>--enable-default-ssp</option> para GCC."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:120
#, xml-text
msgid "<parameter>--disable-nscd</parameter>"
msgstr "<parameter>--disable-nscd</parameter>"

#. type: Content of:
#. <sect1><sect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:122
#, xml-text
msgid "Do not build the name service cache daemon which is no longer used."
msgstr ""
"Não construa o processo de segundo plano de armazenamento temporário do "
"serviço de nomes, o qual não mais é usado."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:128
#, xml-text
msgid "<parameter>libc_cv_slibdir=/usr/lib</parameter>"
msgstr "<parameter>libc_cv_slibdir=/usr/lib</parameter>"

#. type: Content of:
#. <sect1><sect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:130
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"This variable sets the correct library for all systems.  We do not want "
"lib64 to be used."
msgstr ""
"Essa variável configura a biblioteca correta para todos os sistemas. Nós não"
" queremos que a lib64 seja usada."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:137
#, xml-text
msgid "Compile the package:"
msgstr "Compile o pacote:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:139
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput remap=\"make\">make</userinput>"
msgstr "<userinput remap=\"make\">make</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><important><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:142
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"In this section, the test suite for Glibc is considered critical.  Do not "
"skip it under any circumstance."
msgstr ""
"Nesta seção, a suíte de teste para a Glibc é considerada crítica. Não pule-a"
" sob qualquer circunstância."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:146
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Generally a few tests do not pass. The test failures listed below are "
"usually safe to ignore."
msgstr ""
"Geralmente uns poucos testes não passam. As falhas de teste listadas abaixo "
"usualmente são seguras ignorar."

#.  Use remap="make" here to work around a jhalfs issue.
#. <screen>
#. <userinput remap="make">case $(uname -m) in
#.   i?86)   ln -sfnv $PWD/elf/ld-linux.so.2        /lib ;;
#.   x86_64) ln -sfnv $PWD/elf/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2 /lib ;;
#. esac</userinput></screen>
#.     <note><para>The symbolic link above is needed to run the tests at this
#.     stage of building in the chroot environment.  It will be overwritten
#.     in the install phase below.</para></note>
#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:159
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput remap=\"test\">make check</userinput>"
msgstr "<userinput remap=\"test\">make check</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:161
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"You may see some test failures. The Glibc test suite is somewhat dependent "
"on the host system. A few failures out of over 6000 tests can generally be "
"ignored. This is a list of the most common issues seen for recent versions "
"of LFS:"
msgstr ""
"Você possivelmente veja algumas falhas de teste. A suíte de teste da Glibc é"
" de alguma forma dependente do sistema anfitrião. Umas poucas falhas saídas "
"de mais que 6.000 testes geralmente podem ignoradas. Esta é uma lista dos "
"problemas mais comuns vistos para versões recentes do LFS:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:169
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<emphasis>io/tst-lchmod</emphasis> is known to fail in the LFS chroot "
"environment."
msgstr ""
"<emphasis>io/tst-lchmod</emphasis> é conhecido por falhar no ambiente chroot"
" do LFS."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:183
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Some tests, for example <emphasis>nss/tst-nss-files-hosts-multi</emphasis> "
"and <emphasis>nptl/tst-thread-affinity*</emphasis> are known to fail due to "
"a timeout (especially when the system is relatively slow and/or running the "
"test suite with multiple parallel make jobs).  These tests can be identified"
" with:"
msgstr ""
"Alguns testes, por exemplo <emphasis>nss/tst-nss-files-hosts-"
"multi</emphasis> e <emphasis>nptl/tst-thread-affinity*</emphasis> são "
"conhecidos por falharem devido a um tempo limite (especialmente quando o "
"sistema está relativamente lento e (ou) executando a suíte de teste com "
"várias tarefas make paralelas). Esses testes podem ser identificados com:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><itemizedlist><listitem><screen>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:190
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput remap=\"test\">grep \"Timed out\" $(find -name \\*.out)</userinput>"
msgstr "<userinput remap=\"test\">grep \"Timed out\" $(find -name \\*.out)</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:192
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"It's possible to re-run a single test with enlarged timeout with "
"<command>TIMEOUTFACTOR=<replaceable>&lt;factor&gt;</replaceable> make test "
"t=<replaceable>&lt;test name&gt;</replaceable></command>.  For example, "
"<command>TIMEOUTFACTOR=10 make test t=nss/tst-nss-files-hosts-"
"multi</command> will re-run <emphasis>nss/tst-nss-files-hosts-"
"multi</emphasis> with ten times the original timeout."
msgstr ""
"É possível reexecutar um teste com tempo limite aumentado com "
"<command>TIMEOUTFACTOR=<replaceable>&lt;fator&gt;</replaceable> make test "
"t=<replaceable>&lt;nome do teste&gt;</replaceable></command>. Por exemplo, "
"<command>TIMEOUTFACTOR=10 make test t=nss/tst-nss-files-hosts-"
"multi</command> reexecutará <emphasis>nss/tst-nss-files-hosts-"
"multi</emphasis> com dez vezes o tempo limite original."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:203
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Additionally, some tests may fail with a relatively old CPU model (for "
"example <emphasis>elf/tst-cpu-features-cpuinfo</emphasis>) or host kernel "
"version (for example <emphasis>stdlib/tst-arc4random-thread</emphasis>)."
msgstr ""
"Além disso, alguns testes possivelmente falhem com um modelo de CPU "
"relativamente antigo (por exemplo <emphasis>elf/tst-cpu-features-"
"cpuinfo</emphasis>) ou versão do núcleo do anfitrião (por exemplo "
"<emphasis>stdlib/tst-arc4random-thread</emphasis>)."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:211
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Though it is a harmless message, the install stage of Glibc will complain "
"about the absence of <filename>/etc/ld.so.conf</filename>.  Prevent this "
"warning with:"
msgstr ""
"Mesmo sendo uma mensagem inofensiva, o estágio de instalação da Glibc "
"reclamará acerca da ausência do <filename>/etc/ld.so.conf</filename>. Evite "
"esse aviso com:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:215
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput remap=\"install\">touch /etc/ld.so.conf</userinput>"
msgstr "<userinput remap=\"install\">touch /etc/ld.so.conf</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:218
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Fix the Makefile to skip an outdated sanity check that fails with a modern "
"Glibc configuration:"
msgstr ""
"Corrija o Makefile para pular uma verificação de sanidade desatualizada que "
"falha com uma configuração moderna da Glibc:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:221
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput remap=\"install\">sed '/test-installation/s@$(PERL)@echo not "
"running@' -i ../Makefile</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput remap=\"install\">sed '/test-installation/s@$(PERL)@echo not "
"running@' -i ../Makefile</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><important><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:225
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If upgrading Glibc to a new minor version (for example, from Glibc-2.36 to "
"Glibc-&glibc-version;) on a running LFS system, you need to take some extra "
"precautions to avoid breaking the system:"
msgstr ""
"Se atualizar a Glibc para uma nova versão secundária (por exemplo, da "
"Glibc-2.36 para a Glibc-&glibc-version;) em um sistema LFS em execução, "
"[então] você precisará tomar algumas precauções extras para evitar quebrar o"
" sistema:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><important><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:241
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Upgrading Glibc on a LFS system prior to 11.0 (exclusive) is not supported."
"  Rebuild LFS if you are running such an old LFS system but you need a newer"
" Glibc."
msgstr ""
"Atualizar a Glibc em um sistema LFS anterior ao 11.0 (exclusivo) não é "
"suportado. Reconstrua o LFS se você estiver executando um sistema LFS "
"antigo, mas precisar de uma Glibc mais recente."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><important><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:250
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If upgrading on a LFS system prior to 12.0 (exclusive), install "
"<application>Libxcrypt</application> following <xref role='.' linkend='ch-"
"system-libxcrypt'/> In addition to a normal "
"<application>Libxcrypt</application> installation, <emphasis role='bold'>you"
" MUST follow the note in Libxcrypt section to install <filename "
"class='libraryfile'>libcrypt.so.1*</filename> (replacing <filename "
"class='libraryfile'>libcrypt.so.1</filename> from the prior Glibc "
"installation)</emphasis>."
msgstr ""
"Se atualizar em um sistema LFS anterior a 12.0 (exclusivo), [então] instale "
"a <application>Libxcrypt</application> seguindo a <xref role='.' "
"linkend='ch-system-libxcrypt'/> Além de uma instalação normal da "
"<application>Libxcrypt</application>, <emphasis role='bold'>você DEVE seguir"
" a observação na seção Libxcrypt para instalar a <filename "
"class='libraryfile'>libcrypt.so.1*</filename> (substituindo <filename "
"class='libraryfile'>libcrypt.so.1</filename> originária da instalação "
"anterior da Glibc)</emphasis>."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><important><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:269
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If upgrading on a LFS system prior to 12.1 (exclusive), remove the "
"<command>nscd</command> program:"
msgstr ""
"Se atualizar em um sistema LFS anterior ao 12.1 (exclusivo), [então] remova "
"o aplicativo <command>nscd</command>:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><important><itemizedlist><listitem><screen>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:273
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>rm -f /usr/sbin/nscd</userinput>"
msgstr "<userinput>rm -f /usr/sbin/nscd</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><important><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:276
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If this system (prior to LFS 12.1, exclusive) is based on Systemd, it's also"
" needed to disable and stop the <command>nscd</command> service now:"
msgstr ""
"Se esse sistema (anterior ao LFS 12.1, exclusivo) for baseado em Systemd, "
"[então] também é necessário desabilitar e parar o serviço "
"<command>nscd</command> agora:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><important><itemizedlist><listitem><screen>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:281
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>systemctl disable --now nscd</userinput>"
msgstr "<userinput>systemctl disable --now nscd</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><important><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:286
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Upgrade the kernel and reboot if it's older than &min-kernel; (check the "
"current version with <command>uname -r</command>)  or if you want to upgrade"
" it anyway, following <xref linkend='ch-bootable-kernel' role='.'/>"
msgstr ""
"Atualize o núcleo e reinicialize se ele for mais antigo que &min-kernel; "
"(verifique a versão atual com <command>uname -r</command>) ou se quiser "
"atualizá-lo mesmo assim, seguindo a <xref linkend='ch-bootable-kernel' "
"role='.'/>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><important><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:295
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Upgrade the kernel API headers if it's older than &min-kernel; (check the "
"current version with <command>cat /usr/include/linux/version.h</command>)  "
"or if you want to upgrade it anyway, following <xref linkend='ch-tools-"
"linux-headers'/> (but removing <envar>$LFS</envar> from the "
"<command>cp</command> command)."
msgstr ""
"Atualize os cabeçalhos da API do núcleo se forem mais antigos que &min-"
"kernel; (verifique a versão atual com <command>cat "
"/usr/include/linux/version.h</command>) ou se quiser atualizá-los mesmo "
"assim, seguindo a <xref linkend='ch-tools-linux-headers'/> (mas removendo "
"<envar>$LFS</envar> do comando <command>cp</command>)."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><important><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:313
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Perform a <envar>DESTDIR</envar> installation and upgrade the Glibc shared "
"libraries on the system using one single <command>install</command> command:"
msgstr ""
"Realize uma instalação <envar>DESTDIR</envar> e atualize as bibliotecas "
"compartilhadas da Glibc no sistema usando um comando simples "
"<command>install</command>:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><important><itemizedlist><listitem><screen>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:318
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>make DESTDIR=$PWD/dest install\n"
"install -vm755 dest/usr/lib/*.so.* /usr/lib</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>make DESTDIR=$PWD/dest install\n"
"install -vm755 dest/usr/lib/*.so.* /usr/lib</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><important><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:324
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"It's imperative to strictly follow these steps above unless you completely "
"understand what you are doing.  <emphasis role='bold'>Any unexpected "
"deviation may render the system completely unusable.  YOU ARE "
"WARNED.</emphasis>"
msgstr ""
"É obrigatório seguir rigorosamente essas etapas acima, a menos que você "
"entenda completamente o que está fazendo. <emphasis role='bold'>Qualquer "
"desvio inesperado possivelmente torne o sistema completamente desusável. "
"VOCÊ ESTÁ AVISADO(A).</emphasis>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><important><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:331
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Then continue to run the <command>make install</command> command, the "
"<command>sed</command> command against <filename>/usr/bin/ldd</filename>, "
"and the commands to install the locales.  Once they are finished, reboot the"
" system immediately."
msgstr ""
"Em seguida, continue a executar o comando <command>make install</command>, o"
" comando <command>sed</command> contra o <filename>/usr/bin/ldd</filename> e"
" os comandos para instalar as localidades. Assim que estiverem finalizados, "
"reinicialize o sistema imediatamente."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><important><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:339
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"When the system has successfully rebooted, if you are running a LFS system "
"prior to 12.0 (exclusive) where GCC was not built with the "
"<parameter>--disable-fixincludes</parameter> option, move two GCC headers "
"into a better location and remove the stale <quote>fixed</quote> copies of "
"the Glibc headers:"
msgstr ""
"Quando o sistema tiver reinicializado com sucesso, se você estiver "
"executando um sistema LFS anterior à 12.0 (exclusivo) onde o GCC não foi "
"construído com a opção <parameter>--disable-fixincludes</parameter>, mova "
"dois cabeçalhos do GCC para um local melhor e remova as cópias "
"<quote>corrigidas</quote> obsoletas dos cabeçalhos da Glibc:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><important><screen>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:346
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>DIR=$(dirname $(gcc -print-libgcc-file-name))\n"
"[ -e $DIR/include/limits.h ]    || mv $DIR/include{-fixed,}/limits.h\n"
"[ -e $DIR/include/syslimits.h ] || mv $DIR/include{-fixed,}/syslimits.h\n"
"rm -rfv $DIR/include-fixed/*\n"
"unset DIR</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>DIR=$(dirname $(gcc -print-libgcc-file-name))\n"
"[ -e $DIR/include/limits.h ]    || mv $DIR/include{-fixed,}/limits.h\n"
"[ -e $DIR/include/syslimits.h ] || mv $DIR/include{-fixed,}/syslimits.h\n"
"rm -rfv $DIR/include-fixed/*\n"
"unset DIR</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:353
#, xml-text
msgid "Install the package:"
msgstr "Instale o pacote:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:355
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput remap=\"install\">make install</userinput>"
msgstr "<userinput remap=\"install\">make install</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:357
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Fix a hardcoded path to the executable loader in the <command>ldd</command> "
"script:"
msgstr ""
"Corrija um caminho codificado rigidamente para o carregador de executável no"
" script <command>ldd</command>:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:360
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput remap=\"install\">sed '/RTLDLIST=/s@/usr@@g' -i "
"/usr/bin/ldd</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput remap=\"install\">sed '/RTLDLIST=/s@/usr@@g' -i "
"/usr/bin/ldd</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:374
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Next, install the locales that can make the system respond in a different "
"language.  None of these locales are required, but if some of them are "
"missing, the test suites of some packages will skip important test cases."
msgstr ""
"Em seguida, instale as localidades que podem fazer o sistema responder em um"
" idioma diferente. Nenhuma dessas localidades é exigida, mas se algumas "
"delas estiverem ausentes, as suítes de teste de alguns pacotes pularão "
"importantes casos de teste."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:379
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Individual locales can be installed using the <command>localedef</command> "
"program. E.g., the second <command>localedef</command> command below "
"combines the <filename>/usr/share/i18n/locales/cs_CZ</filename> charset-"
"independent locale definition with the "
"<filename>/usr/share/i18n/charmaps/UTF-8.gz</filename> charmap definition "
"and appends the result to the <filename>/usr/lib/locale/locale-"
"archive</filename> file.  The following instructions will install the "
"minimum set of locales necessary for the optimal coverage of tests:"
msgstr ""
"Localidades individuais podem ser instaladas usando-se o programa "
"<command>localedef</command>. Por exemplo, o segundo comando "
"<command>localedef</command> abaixo combina a definição de localidade "
"independente do conjunto de caracteres "
"<filename>/usr/share/i18n/locales/cs_CZ</filename> com a definição de mapa "
"de caracteres <filename>/usr/share/i18n/charmaps/UTF-8.gz</filename> e "
"adiciona o resultado ao arquivo <filename>/usr/lib/locale/locale-"
"archive</filename>. As seguintes instruções instalarão o conjunto mínimo de "
"localidades necessário para a cobertura ótima de testes:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:390
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput remap=\"locale-test\">localedef -i C -f UTF-8 C.UTF-8\n"
"localedef -i cs_CZ -f UTF-8 cs_CZ.UTF-8\n"
"localedef -i de_DE -f ISO-8859-1 de_DE\n"
"localedef -i de_DE@euro -f ISO-8859-15 de_DE@euro\n"
"localedef -i de_DE -f UTF-8 de_DE.UTF-8\n"
"localedef -i el_GR -f ISO-8859-7 el_GR\n"
"localedef -i en_GB -f ISO-8859-1 en_GB\n"
"localedef -i en_GB -f UTF-8 en_GB.UTF-8\n"
"localedef -i en_HK -f ISO-8859-1 en_HK\n"
"localedef -i en_PH -f ISO-8859-1 en_PH\n"
"localedef -i en_US -f ISO-8859-1 en_US\n"
"localedef -i en_US -f UTF-8 en_US.UTF-8\n"
"localedef -i es_ES -f ISO-8859-15 es_ES@euro\n"
"localedef -i es_MX -f ISO-8859-1 es_MX\n"
"localedef -i fa_IR -f UTF-8 fa_IR\n"
"localedef -i fr_FR -f ISO-8859-1 fr_FR\n"
"localedef -i fr_FR@euro -f ISO-8859-15 fr_FR@euro\n"
"localedef -i fr_FR -f UTF-8 fr_FR.UTF-8\n"
"localedef -i is_IS -f ISO-8859-1 is_IS\n"
"localedef -i is_IS -f UTF-8 is_IS.UTF-8\n"
"localedef -i it_IT -f ISO-8859-1 it_IT\n"
"localedef -i it_IT -f ISO-8859-15 it_IT@euro\n"
"localedef -i it_IT -f UTF-8 it_IT.UTF-8\n"
"localedef -i ja_JP -f EUC-JP ja_JP\n"
"localedef -i ja_JP -f UTF-8 ja_JP.UTF-8\n"
"localedef -i nl_NL@euro -f ISO-8859-15 nl_NL@euro\n"
"localedef -i ru_RU -f KOI8-R ru_RU.KOI8-R\n"
"localedef -i ru_RU -f UTF-8 ru_RU.UTF-8\n"
"localedef -i se_NO -f UTF-8 se_NO.UTF-8\n"
"localedef -i ta_IN -f UTF-8 ta_IN.UTF-8\n"
"localedef -i tr_TR -f UTF-8 tr_TR.UTF-8\n"
"localedef -i zh_CN -f GB18030 zh_CN.GB18030\n"
"localedef -i zh_HK -f BIG5-HKSCS zh_HK.BIG5-HKSCS\n"
"localedef -i zh_TW -f UTF-8 zh_TW.UTF-8</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput remap=\"locale-test\">localedef -i C -f UTF-8 C.UTF-8\n"
"localedef -i cs_CZ -f UTF-8 cs_CZ.UTF-8\n"
"localedef -i de_DE -f ISO-8859-1 de_DE\n"
"localedef -i de_DE@euro -f ISO-8859-15 de_DE@euro\n"
"localedef -i de_DE -f UTF-8 de_DE.UTF-8\n"
"localedef -i el_GR -f ISO-8859-7 el_GR\n"
"localedef -i en_GB -f ISO-8859-1 en_GB\n"
"localedef -i en_GB -f UTF-8 en_GB.UTF-8\n"
"localedef -i en_HK -f ISO-8859-1 en_HK\n"
"localedef -i en_PH -f ISO-8859-1 en_PH\n"
"localedef -i en_US -f ISO-8859-1 en_US\n"
"localedef -i en_US -f UTF-8 en_US.UTF-8\n"
"localedef -i es_ES -f ISO-8859-15 es_ES@euro\n"
"localedef -i es_MX -f ISO-8859-1 es_MX\n"
"localedef -i fa_IR -f UTF-8 fa_IR\n"
"localedef -i fr_FR -f ISO-8859-1 fr_FR\n"
"localedef -i fr_FR@euro -f ISO-8859-15 fr_FR@euro\n"
"localedef -i fr_FR -f UTF-8 fr_FR.UTF-8\n"
"localedef -i is_IS -f ISO-8859-1 is_IS\n"
"localedef -i is_IS -f UTF-8 is_IS.UTF-8\n"
"localedef -i it_IT -f ISO-8859-1 it_IT\n"
"localedef -i it_IT -f ISO-8859-15 it_IT@euro\n"
"localedef -i it_IT -f UTF-8 it_IT.UTF-8\n"
"localedef -i ja_JP -f EUC-JP ja_JP\n"
"localedef -i ja_JP -f UTF-8 ja_JP.UTF-8\n"
"localedef -i nl_NL@euro -f ISO-8859-15 nl_NL@euro\n"
"localedef -i ru_RU -f KOI8-R ru_RU.KOI8-R\n"
"localedef -i ru_RU -f UTF-8 ru_RU.UTF-8\n"
"localedef -i se_NO -f UTF-8 se_NO.UTF-8\n"
"localedef -i ta_IN -f UTF-8 ta_IN.UTF-8\n"
"localedef -i tr_TR -f UTF-8 tr_TR.UTF-8\n"
"localedef -i zh_CN -f GB18030 zh_CN.GB18030\n"
"localedef -i zh_HK -f BIG5-HKSCS zh_HK.BIG5-HKSCS\n"
"localedef -i zh_TW -f UTF-8 zh_TW.UTF-8</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:425
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"In addition, install the locale for your own country, language and character"
" set."
msgstr ""
"Adicionalmente, instale a localidade para teu próprio país, idioma e "
"conjunto de caracteres."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:428
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Alternatively, install all the locales listed in the <filename>glibc-&glibc-"
"version;/localedata/SUPPORTED</filename> file (it includes every locale "
"listed above and many more) at once with the following time-consuming "
"command:"
msgstr ""
"Alternativamente, instale todas as localidades listadas no arquivo "
"<filename>glibc-&glibc-version;/localedata/SUPPORTED</filename> (inclui cada"
" localidade listada acima e muitas mais) de uma vez com o seguinte comando "
"consumidor de tempo:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:433
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput remap=\"locale-full\">make localedata/install-locales</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput remap=\"locale-full\">make localedata/install-locales</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:435
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Glibc now uses libidn2 when resolving internationalized domain names.  This "
"is a run time dependency.  If this capability is needed, the instructions "
"for installing libidn2 are in the <ulink url=\"&blfs-"
"book;general/libidn2.html\">BLFS libidn2 page</ulink>."
msgstr ""
"A Glibc agora usa a libidn2 quando resolver nomes internacionalizados de "
"domínio. Essa é uma dependência de tempo de execução. Se essa capacidade for"
" necessária, as instruções para instalar a libidn2 estão na <ulink "
"url=\"&blfs-book;general/libidn2.html\">página da libidn2 do BLFS</ulink>."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:444
#, xml-text
msgid "Configuring Glibc"
msgstr "Configurando a Glibc"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><indexterm><primary>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:447
#, xml-text
msgid "/etc/nsswitch.conf"
msgstr "/etc/nsswitch.conf"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><indexterm><primary>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:451
#, xml-text
msgid "/etc/localtime"
msgstr "/etc/localtime"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><title>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:455
#, xml-text
msgid "Adding nsswitch.conf"
msgstr "Adicionando o nsswitch.conf"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:457
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"The <filename>/etc/nsswitch.conf</filename> file needs to be created because"
" the Glibc defaults do not work well in a networked environment."
msgstr ""
"O arquivo <filename>/etc/nsswitch.conf</filename> precisa ser criado, pois "
"os padrões da Glibc não funcionam bem em um ambiente de rede de comunicação."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:461
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Create a new file <filename>/etc/nsswitch.conf</filename> by running the "
"following:"
msgstr ""
"Crie um novo arquivo <filename>/etc/nsswitch.conf</filename> executando o "
"seguinte:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:464
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>cat &gt; /etc/nsswitch.conf &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Begin /etc/nsswitch.conf\n"
"\n"
"passwd: files\n"
"group: files\n"
"shadow: files\n"
"\n"
"hosts: files dns\n"
"networks: files\n"
"\n"
"protocols: files\n"
"services: files\n"
"ethers: files\n"
"rpc: files\n"
"\n"
"# End /etc/nsswitch.conf</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>cat &gt; /etc/nsswitch.conf &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Inicia /etc/nsswitch.conf\n"
"\n"
"passwd: files\n"
"group: files\n"
"shadow: files\n"
"\n"
"hosts: files dns\n"
"networks: files\n"
"\n"
"protocols: files\n"
"services: files\n"
"ethers: files\n"
"rpc: files\n"
"\n"
"# Termina /etc/nsswitch.conf</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:482
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>cat &gt; /etc/nsswitch.conf &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Begin /etc/nsswitch.conf\n"
"\n"
"passwd: files systemd\n"
"group: files systemd\n"
"shadow: files systemd\n"
"\n"
"hosts: mymachines resolve [!UNAVAIL=return] files myhostname dns\n"
"networks: files\n"
"\n"
"protocols: files\n"
"services: files\n"
"ethers: files\n"
"rpc: files\n"
"\n"
"# End /etc/nsswitch.conf</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>cat &gt; /etc/nsswitch.conf &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Inicia /etc/nsswitch.conf\n"
"\n"
"passwd: files systemd\n"
"group: files systemd\n"
"shadow: files systemd\n"
"\n"
"hosts: mymachines resolve [!UNAVAIL=return] files myhostname dns\n"
"networks: files\n"
"\n"
"protocols: files\n"
"services: files\n"
"ethers: files\n"
"rpc: files\n"
"\n"
"# Termina /etc/nsswitch.conf</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><title>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:503
#, xml-text
msgid "Adding Time Zone Data"
msgstr "Adicionando Dados de Fuso Horário"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:505
#, xml-text
msgid "Install and set up the time zone data with the following:"
msgstr "Instale e configure os dados de fuso horário com o seguinte:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:506
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>tar -xf ../../tzdata&tzdata-version;.tar.gz\n"
"\n"
"ZONEINFO=/usr/share/zoneinfo\n"
"mkdir -pv $ZONEINFO/{posix,right}\n"
"\n"
"for tz in etcetera southamerica northamerica europe africa antarctica  \\\n"
"          asia australasia backward; do\n"
"    zic -L /dev/null   -d $ZONEINFO       ${tz}\n"
"    zic -L /dev/null   -d $ZONEINFO/posix ${tz}\n"
"    zic -L leapseconds -d $ZONEINFO/right ${tz}\n"
"done\n"
"\n"
"cp -v zone.tab zone1970.tab iso3166.tab $ZONEINFO\n"
"zic -d $ZONEINFO -p America/New_York\n"
"unset ZONEINFO tz</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>tar -xf ../../tzdata&tzdata-version;.tar.gz\n"
"\n"
"ZONEINFO=/usr/share/zoneinfo\n"
"mkdir -pv $ZONEINFO/{posix,right}\n"
"\n"
"for tz in etcetera southamerica northamerica europe africa antarctica  \\\n"
"          asia australasia backward; do\n"
"    zic -L /dev/null   -d $ZONEINFO       ${tz}\n"
"    zic -L /dev/null   -d $ZONEINFO/posix ${tz}\n"
"    zic -L leapseconds -d $ZONEINFO/right ${tz}\n"
"done\n"
"\n"
"cp -v zone.tab zone1970.tab iso3166.tab $ZONEINFO\n"
"zic -d $ZONEINFO -p America/New_York\n"
"unset ZONEINFO tz</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><variablelist><title>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:523
#, xml-text
msgid "The meaning of the zic commands:"
msgstr "O significado dos comandos zic:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:526
#, xml-text
msgid "<parameter>zic -L /dev/null ...</parameter>"
msgstr "<parameter>zic -L /dev/null ...</parameter>"

#. type: Content of:
#. <sect1><sect2><sect3><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:528
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"This creates posix time zones without any leap seconds.  It is conventional "
"to put these in both <filename class=\"directory\">zoneinfo</filename> and "
"<filename class=\"directory\">zoneinfo/posix</filename>. It is necessary to "
"put the POSIX time zones in <filename "
"class=\"directory\">zoneinfo</filename>, otherwise various test suites will "
"report errors. On an embedded system, where space is tight and you do not "
"intend to ever update the time zones, you could save 1.9 MB by not using the"
" <filename class=\"directory\">posix</filename> directory, but some "
"applications or test suites might produce some failures."
msgstr ""
"Isso cria fusos horários posix sem quaisquer segundos bissextos. É "
"convencional colocá-los em ambos <filename "
"class=\"directory\">zoneinfo</filename> e <filename "
"class=\"directory\">zoneinfo/posix</filename>. É necessário colocar os fusos"
" horários POSIX em <filename class=\"directory\">zoneinfo</filename>, do "
"contrário várias suítes de teste reportarão erros. Em um sistema embarcado, "
"onde o espaço é apertado e você não pretende nunca atualizar os fusos "
"horários, você poderia economizar 1,9 MB não usando o diretório <filename "
"class=\"directory\">posix</filename>, mas alguns aplicativos ou suítes de "
"teste poderiam produzir algumas falhas."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:542
#, xml-text
msgid "<parameter>zic -L leapseconds ...</parameter>"
msgstr "<parameter>zic -L leapseconds ...</parameter>"

#. type: Content of:
#. <sect1><sect2><sect3><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:544
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"This creates right time zones, including leap seconds. On an embedded "
"system, where space is tight and you do not intend to ever update the time "
"zones, or care about the correct time, you could save 1.9MB by omitting the "
"<filename class=\"directory\">right</filename> directory."
msgstr ""
"Isso cria fusos horários corretos, incluindo segundos bissextos. Em um "
"sistema embarcado, onde o espaço é apertado e você não pretende nunca "
"atualizar os fusos horários ou se importa com a hora correta, você poderia "
"economizar 1,9 MB omitindo o diretório <filename "
"class=\"directory\">right</filename>."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:552
#, xml-text
msgid "<parameter>zic ... -p ...</parameter>"
msgstr "<parameter>zic ... -p ...</parameter>"

#. type: Content of:
#. <sect1><sect2><sect3><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:554
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"This creates the <filename>posixrules</filename> file. We use New York "
"because POSIX requires the daylight saving time rules to be in accordance "
"with US rules."
msgstr ""
"Isso cria o arquivo <filename>posixrules</filename>. Nós usamos New York, "
"pois POSIX exige que as regras de horário de verão estejam de acordo com "
"regras dos Estados Unidos da América do Norte."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:562
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"One way to determine the local time zone is to run the following script:"
msgstr ""
"Uma maneira para determinar o fuso horário local é a de executar o seguinte "
"conjunto de comandos sequenciais:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:565
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>tzselect</userinput>"
msgstr "<userinput>tzselect</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:567
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"After answering a few questions about the location, the script will output "
"the name of the time zone (e.g., <emphasis>America/Edmonton</emphasis>). "
"There are also some other possible time zones listed in <filename "
"class='directory'>/usr/share/zoneinfo</filename> such as "
"<emphasis>Canada/Eastern</emphasis> or <emphasis>EST5EDT</emphasis> that are"
" not identified by the script but can be used."
msgstr ""
"Depois de responder à umas poucas perguntas a respeito do local, o conjunto "
"de comandos sequenciais retornará o nome do fuso horário (por exemplo, "
"<emphasis>America/Edmonton</emphasis>). Existem também alguns outros "
"possíveis fusos horários listados em <filename "
"class='directory'>/usr/share/zoneinfo</filename>, tais como "
"<emphasis>Canada/Eastern</emphasis> ou <emphasis>EST5EDT</emphasis> que não "
"são identificados pelo conjunto de comandos sequenciais, mas podem ser "
"usados."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:575
#, xml-text
msgid "Then create the <filename>/etc/localtime</filename> file by running:"
msgstr "Então crie o arquivo <filename>/etc/localtime</filename> executando:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:578
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>ln -sfv "
"/usr/share/zoneinfo/<replaceable>&lt;xxx&gt;</replaceable> "
"/etc/localtime</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>ln -sfv "
"/usr/share/zoneinfo/<replaceable>&lt;xxx&gt;</replaceable> "
"/etc/localtime</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:580
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Replace <replaceable>&lt;xxx&gt;</replaceable> with the name of the time "
"zone selected (e.g., Canada/Eastern)."
msgstr ""
"Substitua <replaceable>&lt;xxx&gt;</replaceable> pelo nome do fuso horário "
"selecionado (por exemplo, Canada/Eastern)."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><title>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:586
#, xml-text
msgid "Configuring the Dynamic Loader"
msgstr "Configurando o Carregador Dinâmico"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><indexterm><primary>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:589
#, xml-text
msgid "/etc/ld.so.conf"
msgstr "/etc/ld.so.conf"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:592
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"By default, the dynamic loader (<filename class=\"libraryfile\">/lib/ld-"
"linux.so.2</filename>) searches through <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/usr/lib</filename> for dynamic libraries that are "
"needed by programs as they are run. However, if there are libraries in "
"directories other than <filename class=\"directory\">/usr/lib</filename>, "
"these need to be added to the <filename>/etc/ld.so.conf</filename> file in "
"order for the dynamic loader to find them. Two directories that are commonly"
" known to contain additional libraries are <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/usr/local/lib</filename> and <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/opt/lib</filename>, so add those directories to the "
"dynamic loader's search path."
msgstr ""
"Por padrão, o carregador dinâmico (<filename class=\"libraryfile\">/lib/ld-"
"linux.so.2</filename>) procura em <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/usr/lib</filename> por bibliotecas dinâmicas que são "
"necessárias para aplicativos assim que são executados. Entretanto, se "
"existirem bibliotecas em outros diretórios diferentes do <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/usr/lib</filename>, esses precisam ser adicionados ao "
"arquivo <filename>/etc/ld.so.conf</filename> para a finalidade de que o "
"carregador dinâmico encontre elas. Dois diretórios que são comumente "
"conhecidos por conterem bibliotecas adicionais são <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/usr/local/lib</filename> e <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/opt/lib</filename>; então adicione esses diretórios ao "
"caminho de busca do carregador dinâmico."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:605
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Create a new file <filename>/etc/ld.so.conf</filename> by running the "
"following:"
msgstr ""
"Crie um novo arquivo <filename>/etc/ld.so.conf</filename> executando o "
"seguinte:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:608
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>cat &gt; /etc/ld.so.conf &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Begin /etc/ld.so.conf\n"
"/usr/local/lib\n"
"/opt/lib\n"
"</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>cat &gt; /etc/ld.so.conf &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Inicia /etc/ld.so.conf\n"
"/usr/local/lib\n"
"/opt/lib\n"
"</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:615
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If desired, the dynamic loader can also search a directory and include the "
"contents of files found there.  Generally the files in this include "
"directory are one line specifying the desired library path.  To add this "
"capability run the following commands:"
msgstr ""
"Se desejado, o carregador dinâmico também pode pesquisar um diretório e "
"incluir o conteúdo de arquivos encontrados lá. Geralmente os arquivos nesse "
"diretório include são uma linha especificando o caminho de biblioteca "
"desejado. Para adicionar essa capacidade, execute os seguintes comandos:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: lfs-en/chapter08/glibc.xml:620
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>cat &gt;&gt; /etc/ld.so.conf &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Add an include directory\n"
"include /etc/ld.so.conf.d/*.conf\n"
"</literal>\n"
"EOF\n"
"mkdir -pv /etc/ld.so.conf.d</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>cat &gt;&gt; /etc/ld.so.conf &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Adiciona um diretório de inclusão\n"
"include /etc/ld.so.conf.d/*.conf\n"
"</literal>\n"
"EOF\n"
"mkdir -pv /etc/ld.so.conf.d</userinput>"

